
# 🔢 NumPy — Data Analytics Notes

> ⚡ NumPy = Fast arrays + Math + The backbone of every data analytics library.

---

🚀 Setup
```bash
pip install numpy
import numpy as np
```

---

📐 Arrays
```python
np.array([1, 2, 3])            # 1D
np.array([[1,2],[3,4]])        # 2D
np.zeros((3,3))                # All zeros
np.arange(0, 10, 2)           # [0,2,4,6,8]
np.random.rand(3, 3)          # Random matrix
```

---

⚙️ Operations
```python
a = np.array([10, 20, 30])
a + 5   # [15, 25, 35]
a * 2   # [20, 40, 60]
a ** 2  # [100, 400, 900]
```

---

🔍 Indexing
```python
arr = np.array([10, 20, 30, 40, 50])
arr[0]        # 10
arr[1:4]      # [20, 30, 40]
arr[arr > 25] # [30, 40, 50]  ← Boolean indexing 🔥
```

---

📊 Statistics (Most Used in Analytics)
```python
data = np.array([5, 10, 15, 20, 25])

np.mean(data)    # 15.0
np.median(data)  # 15.0
np.std(data)     # 7.07
np.min(data)     # 5
np.max(data)     # 25
np.sum(data)     # 75
```

---

🛠️ Real Analytics Tricks

**Normalize data:**
```python
norm = (data - data.min()) / (data.max() - data.min())
```

**Remove NaN:**
```python
clean = data[~np.isnan(data)]
```

**Find outliers:**
```python
filtered = data[np.abs(data - np.mean(data)) < 2 * np.std(data)]
```

